---
description: Apply the verified development, commit and remote-handoff loop
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- One branch represents one stable work item or vertical increment.
- Use the test-driven-development skill for production changes.
- Establish a failing test or executable reproduction before behavior changes.
- Run focused tests, then affected contract/integration/security/architecture
  suites.
- Never edit generated output directly or weaken a test to pass.
- Commit coherent verified units on the same branch; do not create a branch per
  commit.
- The developer agent is the sole branch writer.
- The remote agent validates an exact pushed SHA and never edits code.
- Record commit, PR, commands and exact-SHA evidence in the engineering ledgers.
- Open an ADR instead of improvising a frozen semantic change.
